# Variable Naming: camelCase

All variable names must use **camelCase**. Do not use snake_case, PascalCase, or SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for variables.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const user_name = "kim";
const UserName = "kim";
const USER_NAME = "kim";

// ✅ GOOD
const userName = "kim";
```

Applies to:
- Local variables
- Function parameters
- Object properties when naming in new code
- Destructured bindings

Exceptions (keep conventional casing):
- React components and classes: PascalCase
- True constants / env-style enums when already established: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE only if the codebase already uses that pattern for constants
